  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FROM KEY 2 TO KEY 1: IMPROVING THE POPULATION STATUS OF BLACK RHINOS IN THE NORTH WEST PROVINCE, SOUTH AFRICA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN PILANESBERG NATURE RESERVE AND MADIKWE NATURE RESERVE IN THE NORTH WEST PROVINCE OF SOUTH AFRICA BY IMPROVING SECURITY AND MANAGEMENT IN BOTH RESERVES FOR THE PROTECTION OF RHINOCEROS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITATS BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) IMPROVING RHINOCEROS TRACKING (2) INCREASING PROTECTION (3) UPGRADING STAFF ACCOMMODATIONS AND (4) SUPPORTING DETECTION DOGS TO INCREASE DETECTION OF POACHERS AND REDUCE THE ILLEGAL POACHING OF RHINOCEROS.</narrative>
  </description>
